@how own mechanism: Allow emergent clusters to attach lightweight economic tools (mutual aid, microcredit, resource maps) to relational arcs. (source: this pattern's ! conclusion line; L7 rationale-backfill, zai-1, 2026-09-05)

! conclusion: 
  Allow emergent clusters to attach lightweight economic tools (mutual aid, microcredit, resource maps) to relational arcs.

  + context: You are exploring how narrative connections can be paired with lightweight economic tools so relational meaning aligns with material mutual support. This does not apply when there is no willingness to manage shared resources. Treat this as future work until core linking is validated.

  + IF:
    Atomised interventions and isolated acts of generosity rarely create durable resilience.

  + HOWEVER:
    Story systems that operate purely at the narrative level ignore material alignment.

  + THEN:
    Allow emergent clusters to attach lightweight economic tools (mutual aid, microcredit, resource maps) to relational arcs.

  + BECAUSE:
    When narrative resonance aligns with economic mutuality, the manifold becomes regenerative rather than extractive.

  + NEXT-STEPS:
    next[Prototype one mutual-aid link attached to an existing story cluster.]
    next[Define a lightweight resource map schema for shared contributions.]
    next[Define a success metric (e.g., mutual-aid participation rises after linking) and a falsifying observation.]
    next[Identify one small-scale pilot (e.g., one community media org linking to a few peers) to test feasibility.]
